.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt XCRUN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xcrun
.Nd locate and run selected developer tools
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -run
.Ar tool
.Op Ar argument ...
.Nm
.Fl -find
.Ar tool
.Nm
.Fl -show-sdk-path
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
locates tools in the selected developer directory's
.Pa usr/bin
and executes them with their arguments and environment unchanged.
It does not search
.Ev PATH .
A tool name must be a basename other than
.Ql .
or
.Ql .. ,
and must not start with a dash.
The tool must resolve to an executable regular file.
.Pp
A nonempty
.Ev DEVELOPER_DIR
selects the developer directory first.
Otherwise the target of
.Pa /var/db/xcode_select_link
is used.
Only an absent selection permits the default
.Pa /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools .
An invalid selection fails without falling through.
.Pp
.Fl -find
prints the executable path without running it.
.Fl -show-sdk-path
prints
.Pa /
without reading a selection.
.Fl -help
prints usage.
These queries accept no additional arguments.
.Pp
The hard links
.Nm swift ,
.Nm swiftc ,
.Nm swift-build ,
.Nm swift-test ,
.Nm swift-run ,
.Nm swift-package ,
and
.Nm sourcekit-lsp
run the corresponding selected tool, forwarding every argument.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Selection, lookup and execution errors return 1; syntax errors return 2.
After execution, the selected tool controls the exit status.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xcode-select 1
.Sh NOTES
The source directory's README.md specifies the supported contract.
Other Apple options, SDK discovery and toolchain selection are not implemented.
